{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cg6VhqQJsNa8RPumjyUbJ", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "```\nTable 3 reports the estimates, and they point to a consistent role for reviewer identity. In column 2, the coefficient on the identity-disclosed indicator is 0.18 (SE = 0.04). It remains sizable after we add product fixed effects in column 3, at 0.15 (SE = 0.05). Identity also conditions on who is speaking: the interaction with reviewer tenure is 0.09 (SE = 0.03) in column 4. Star rating matters throughout, with a coefficient of 0.42 (SE = 0.02) across all specifications, yet identity adds to it rather than merely echoing it. R-squared rises from 0.31 to 0.47 across the columns. All coefficients are significant at the 1% level except the interaction, which is significant at the 5% level.\n```\n\nI kept every number and the column order unchanged, and the paragraph has no citations. Two edits are worth checking, since they go slightly beyond rewording:\n\n- \"Identity adds to it rather than merely echoing it\" is my interpretive gloss on the identity and star-rating coefficients. If you'd rather not make that claim in the results section, delete that clause.\n- \"Identity also conditions on who is speaking\" frames the tenure interaction as moderation. Cut it if tenure isn't meant to be read that way in your theory."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1881, "cache_read_input_tokens": 1496, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1881}, "output_tokens": 2, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "19b6103d-cbfc-505f-8dc1-c40cc8379cf6", "uuid": "45eacb3c-0791-4618-acbe-a395c7c2cb62",